# L §5.3: "Two items of one label, or of one target at the same stated keys, with overlapping spans in one version
# are refused (LOAD-OVERLAP); rows at different stated keys are ordered by precedence (§4.6 step 3)."  n = 1
# states no key, n[a] = 2 states one, both in one version over one span: n[a] = 2 (the row that states more keys,
# §4.6 step 3.2), n[b] = 1.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"
index ks = [a, b]
input n[k in ks]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2015-11..
  known 2016-01-01
  n = 1
  n[a] = 2

ask q: n[a], n[b] law 2016-02-01
=== expect
q: (2, 1)
  law date 2016-02-01, cut 2016-03-01
